Then the Truth, glory be to Him, says:

{But We produced generations, and the time span lengthened for them. And you were not dwelling among the people of Madyan, reciting to them Our verses, but We were the ones who sent (messengers).}

The people of Madyan are the people of Shu'ayb, peace be upon him. They were occupied with reading, so the Exalted said to His Prophet Muhammad, may Allah bless him and grant him peace: ﴿And you were not dwelling…﴾ [al-Qasas: 45], meaning: residing. ﴿…among the people of Madyan, reciting to them Our verses…﴾ [al-Qasas: 45], meaning: reciting as a student recites to his teacher so that the teacher may correct him. ﴿But We were the ones who sent (messengers)﴾ [al-Qasas: 45], meaning: that all the messages come from Us, whether to one who reads or to one who is unlettered.

Then the Truth, glorified is He, says:

{And let them not turn you away from the signs of Allah after they have been revealed to you. Call to your Lord, and do not be among the polytheists.}

His saying, exalted is He: ﴿And let them not turn you away...﴾ [al-Qasas: 87], meaning: let not the polytheists divert you or prevent you, ﴿from the signs of Allah﴾ [al-Qasas: 87], meaning: from reciting them and conveying them to the people. And His saying: ﴿and do not be among the polytheists﴾ [al-Qasas: 87] is also included in "It is you I mean, but hear, O neighbour" (iyyaka a'ni wa-isma'i ya jarah), because the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) is far removed from polytheism and is not suspected of it.
